    "title": "【对话场景】表达请求和命令",
    "text": "第十一单元\n第一课\n【对话场景】表达请求和命令\n——Come in, Amy.\n艾米，进来。\nShut the door, please.\n请把门关上。\nThis bedroom is very untidy.\n这卧室太不整洁了。\n——What must I do, Mrs. Jones?\n有什么是我必须做的呢，琼斯太太？\n——Open the window and air the room.\n把窗户打开，给房间通风。\nThen put these clothes in the wardrobe.\n把这些衣服放进衣橱里。\nThen make the bed.\n再把床整理一下。\nDust the dressing table.\n掸掉梳妆台上的灰尘。\nThen sweep the floor.\n然后把地扫一下。\n• 动词原形作祈使句的用法\n◦ 祈使语气表示直接的命令、建议、劝告或邀请\n◦ 省略了主语 you，采用动词原形\n• air the room 的用法\n◦ air 作动词用，给······通风\n◦ air 的名词意思是空气\n◦ 同义替换：ventilate the room\n▪ ventilate 动词，给······通风\n◦ dust the table 也为相似的用法\n• put sth. in... 的用法\n◦ 把某物放进某地方\n◦ 相当于 put sth. into，into 更强调这个过程\n◦ put 有很多常用的搭配\n▪ put away 把······放起来\n▪ put out 把······熄灭\n▪ put through 接通电话\n第二课\n【语法点拨】有态度的情态动词\n情态动词本身具有有一定的词义，表达着说话人的情感、态度或语气。因为词义不完\n全，情态动词不能单独作谓语, 只能与实义动词原形一起构成谓语。\n常用的情态动词 can (could), may (might), must, need, ought to, dare (dared),\nshall (should), will (would)\n• 表示推测及可能性\n◦ may，might，can, could, will, would 表示“可能”\n◦ shall, should 用于表示“应该会”\n◦ must 用于表示“必定”，“必会“\n◦ ought to 表“应该会”\n• 表示意愿及打算\n◦ will, would 表示打算做某事\n◦ shall, should 表示应该做某事\n◦ would，should 要比 will，shall 更委婉\n• 表示态度及许可\n◦ must 表示必须做，否定形式是 mustn't 千万不要做\n◦ ought to 表示应该做，语气没有 must 强烈\n第三课\n【单词串烧】\n• shut [ʃʌt] v. 关门\n• bedroom ['bedrum, -ru:m] n. 卧室\n• untidy [ˌʌn'taidi] a. 乱，不整齐\n• must [mʌst] modal verb. 必须，应该\n• open ['əupən] v. 打开\n• air [eə] v. 使…通风，换换空气\n• put [put] v. 放置\n• clothes [kləuðz] n. 衣服\n• wardrobe ['wɔ:drəub] n. 大衣柜\n• dust [dʌst] v. 掸掉灰尘\n• sweep [swi:p] v. 扫\n• empty ['empti] v. 倒空，使…变空\n• read [ri:d] v. 读\n• sharpen ['ʃɑ:pən] v. 削尖，使锋利\n• put on [ˌput'ɔn] 穿上\n• take off 脱掉\n• turn on [tə:n ɔn] 开(电灯)\n• turn off 关(电灯)",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "第十一单元"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "第一课"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "【对话场景】表达请求和命令"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "——Come in, Amy."
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "艾米，进来。"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Shut the door, please."
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "请把门关上。"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "This bedroom is very untidy."
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "这卧室太不整洁了。"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "——What must I do, Mrs. Jones?"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "有什么是我必须做的呢，琼斯太太？"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "——Open the window and air the room."
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "把窗户打开，给房间通风。"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Then put these clothes in the wardrobe."
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "把这些衣服放进衣橱里。"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Then make the bed."
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "再把床整理一下。"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Dust the dressing table."
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "掸掉梳妆台上的灰尘。"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Then sweep the floor."
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "然后把地扫一下。"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "• 动词原形作祈使句的用法"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "◦ 祈使语气表示直接的命令、建议、劝告或邀请"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "◦ 省略了主语 you，采用动词原形"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "• air the room 的用法"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "◦ air 作动词用，给······通风"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "◦ air 的名词意思是空气"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "◦ 同义替换：ventilate the room"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "▪ ventilate 动词，给······通风"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "◦ dust the table 也为相似的用法"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "• put sth. in... 的用法"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "◦ 把某物放进某地方"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "◦ 相当于 put sth. into，into 更强调这个过程"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "◦ put 有很多常用的搭配"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "▪ put away 把······放起来"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "▪ put out 把······熄灭"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "▪ put through 接通电话"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "第二课"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "【语法点拨】有态度的情态动词"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "情态动词本身具有有一定的词义，表达着说话人的情感、态度或语气。因为词义不完"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "全，情态动词不能单独作谓语, 只能与实义动词原形一起构成谓语。"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "常用的情态动词 can (could), may (might), must, need, ought to, dare (dared),"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "shall (should), will (would)"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "• 表示推测及可能性"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "◦ may，might，can, could, will, would 表示“可能”"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "◦ shall, should 用于表示“应该会”"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "◦ must 用于表示“必定”，“必会“"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "◦ ought to 表“应该会”"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "• 表示意愿及打算"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "◦ will, would 表示打算做某事"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "◦ shall, should 表示应该做某事"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "◦ would，should 要比 will，shall 更委婉"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "• 表示态度及许可"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "◦ must 表示必须做，否定形式是 mustn't 千万不要做"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "◦ ought to 表示应该做，语气没有 must 强烈"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "第三课"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "【单词串烧】"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "• shut [ʃʌt] v. 关门"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "• bedroom ['bedrum, -ru:m] n. 卧室"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "• untidy [ˌʌn'taidi] a. 乱，不整齐"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "• must [mʌst] modal verb. 必须，应该"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "• open ['əupən] v. 打开"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "• air [eə] v. 使…通风，换换空气"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "• put [put] v. 放置"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "• clothes [kləuðz] n. 衣服"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "• wardrobe ['wɔ:drəub] n. 大衣柜"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "• dust [dʌst] v. 掸掉灰尘"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "• sweep [swi:p] v. 扫"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "• empty ['empti] v. 倒空，使…变空"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "• read [ri:d] v. 读"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "• sharpen ['ʃɑ:pən] v. 削尖，使锋利"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "• put on [ˌput'ɔn] 穿上"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "• take off 脱掉"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "• turn on [tə:n ɔn] 开(电灯)"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "text": "• turn off 关(电灯)"
      }
    ]
  },
